  "title": "COP31 Runs Into Overtime Over Fossil Fuels #shorts",
  "description": "The UN climate talks in Antalya, Türkiye, ran past their Friday deadline as nearly 200 countries clashed over fossil fuels and climate finance. Thursday's revised draft deal no longer mentions fossil fuels and dropped a $120 billion adaptation finance target, several outlets report. Countries including France, Panama and the Solomon Islands wrote that any deal must include \"a clear transition away from fossil fuels\"; Panama's environment minister Juan Carlos Navarro threatened a formal objection. Reports say resistance is led by producers including Saudi Arabia and Russia. COP31 President Murat Kurum: \"We are close to the finish line, but we are not there yet.\" A new draft was expected on Saturday.\n\nSources: The National, Forbes, The Independent (via Yahoo News), 24NewsHD, Yahoo News Australia, Reuters (Nov 16 draft) (based on search-result excerpts). Map locations are for orientation.\n\n#climate #cop31 #fossilfuels #climatechange #antalya",
